WEBVTT

00:09.561 --> 00:11.601
Many companies still treat AI as

00:11.601 --> 00:14.080
magic. By the tools and the value

00:14.080 --> 00:15.361
will follow.

00:15.361 --> 00:17.601
It does not. Value comes from a

00:17.601 --> 00:20.561
method, a deliberate lean AI

00:20.561 --> 00:21.641
transformation.

00:21.882 --> 00:23.562
On the productivity side, done

00:23.562 --> 00:25.921
well, lean AI makes work more

00:25.921 --> 00:28.602
efficient, simpler admin tasks,

00:28.602 --> 00:30.482
less waste in every workflow,

00:30.482 --> 00:33.482
tangible ROI, and it enables

00:33.482 --> 00:35.682
innovation, knowledge capture at

00:35.682 --> 00:38.522
scale, a more agile, skills-based

00:38.522 --> 00:39.642
organization.

00:39.643 --> 00:41.683
On the cultural side, it is not

00:41.683 --> 00:43.643
magic either. We put people at

00:43.643 --> 00:45.883
the core of every redesign. We

00:45.883 --> 00:47.843
define where human value lies and

00:47.843 --> 00:49.763
we recognize it at individual and

00:49.763 --> 00:51.043
team level.

00:51.043 --> 00:52.803
AI augments that work so people

00:52.803 --> 00:54.723
focus on what gives it purpose.

00:54.723 --> 00:56.363
The time AI freeze goes to

00:56.363 --> 00:58.002
collective moments.

00:58.002 --> 01:00.203
And AI becomes a personal tutor.

01:00.203 --> 01:01.803
It helps each of us learn and

01:01.803 --> 01:03.082
helps leaders grow as team

01:03.082 --> 01:03.963
coaches.

01:04.084 --> 01:07.004
Only 6% of companies are AI high

01:07.004 --> 01:08.684
performers and they are three

01:08.684 --> 01:10.124
times more likely to have

01:10.124 --> 01:11.803
fundamentally redesigned their

01:11.803 --> 01:14.244
workflows around AI instead of

01:14.244 --> 01:16.763
automating what already existed.

01:16.763 --> 01:19.643
The gap is not the technology. It

01:19.643 --> 01:20.804
is the method.

01:21.004 --> 01:22.925
So, how does the Lean AI method

01:22.925 --> 01:25.644
work? Step one is vision. Just

01:25.644 --> 01:27.765
like Lean, start with the vision,

01:27.765 --> 01:30.444
not the technology. Write the 2030

01:30.444 --> 01:32.404
headlines you want to read and

01:32.404 --> 01:33.645
share them.

01:33.645 --> 01:35.564
Then work backwards to today and

01:35.564 --> 01:37.645
identify the processes impacted.

01:37.845 --> 01:39.966
Step two is focus. Map these

01:39.966 --> 01:42.405
processes on the lean AI matrix,

01:42.405 --> 01:44.925
data maturity, adoption simplicity

01:44.925 --> 01:46.846
and impact. Never transform

01:46.846 --> 01:48.526
everything at once. That is how

01:48.526 --> 01:50.205
transformations fail.

01:50.205 --> 01:51.766
The matrix shows where the value

01:51.766 --> 01:53.765
is ready today and which gaps you

01:53.765 --> 01:55.486
must close before you scale.

01:55.487 --> 01:58.287
Step three is reinvent. Put AI on

01:58.287 --> 01:59.846
a bad process and you only

01:59.846 --> 02:01.487
accelerate tasks that create no

02:01.487 --> 02:02.647
value.

02:02.647 --> 02:04.447
So, we use value stream mapping

02:04.447 --> 02:06.407
to redesign the whole flow, not

02:06.407 --> 02:08.246
just the task. Wave one

02:08.246 --> 02:10.727
accelerates the process. Wave two

02:10.727 --> 02:13.407
reinvent it and turns admin time

02:13.407 --> 02:15.447
into human time. Simplify the

02:15.447 --> 02:18.006
transaction, elevate the moment.

02:18.006 --> 02:20.167
This may seem like common sense,

02:20.167 --> 02:22.207
but is your organization doing it

02:22.207 --> 02:24.006
in a structured and systematic

02:24.006 --> 02:24.926
way?

02:24.926 --> 02:27.007
And do you feel able to do it.

02:27.258 --> 02:29.338
Once the method is in place, one

02:29.338 --> 02:30.937
challenge remains.

02:30.937 --> 02:33.498
How do we see and steer our

02:33.498 --> 02:34.738
workforce?

02:34.738 --> 02:37.058
That is the last shift. See you

02:37.058 --> 02:38.298
in the final episode.
